      "id": "r2",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "tastes of his times. For a similar comparison between a minister",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "and a poet, see Mud. IV. 2; Sis. XI. 6.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r3",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 17. परिचरितव्याः—should be attended upon. यद्यपि &c.—",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "i. e. if they do not give special instruction &c. न—It will be",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "better to read नो to suit the metre. स्वैरकथाः—randam talk;",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "स्वेन ईर्ते ईरति वा । पचाद्यच् । शास्त्राणि—precepts, information that",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "can be safely relied upon.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 18. कन्दुकपातेन—a curious phrase probably used for the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "metre; the regular one would be कन्दुकपातं पतति, in the manner",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "of the fall of a ball i. e. to rise again. केन तुल्यं कन्दुकपातेन कन्दु-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "कपातवत् यथा कन्दुकः पतन्नुत्पतति । Râmarshi. Cf. प्रायेण साधुवृत्तानां &c.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "supra sl. 86. आर्यः—An honourable man, a man of merit. मृत्पिण्ड-",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "a lump of clay, which remains sticking to the ground and",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "never rises up.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 19. अवकर m. sweepings, dust: from अवकृ + अ ( अप् ,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "अवकीर्यते इति ). कृकवाकु—कृकेण गलेन वक्तीति a cock. हंसः—a word",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "of the पृषोदरादि class; fr. हन् to go or हम् ; भवेद्वर्णागमात् हंसः ( the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "न् or म् comes in irregularly ). Fig. अप्रस्तुतप्रशंसा.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r6",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 20. मदभिन्न V. l.—In this case गण्ड must be taken in the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "sense of cheeks, and करट the frontal globes. निद्रालसाः—dull with",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "the nightly sleep. वीणा &c.—For the idea expressed here, comp.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "Kir. I. 38. and Rag. V. 65. सुरलोकदेव—the lord of the world",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "of gods i. e. Indra; or it may mean the gods of heaven. सदृशं—",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "qualifies तदैश्वर्यं understood. विस्फूर्जितं—properly a flash of light-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "ning; hence manifestation. Construe नागाः निद्रालसाः तिष्ठन्ति इति",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "यत् &c.—When the relative stands for a whole sentence such as",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "is represented by ‘that’ in English, it is always used in the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "sing. number and neuter gender. See Apte’s Guide. § 25. The",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "fig. is उदात्त which is described as उदात्तं वस्तुनः संपत् the descrip-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 12,
          "text": "tion of the excellence of a thing.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r7",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 21. परोपकारित्वम्—परस्य उपकरोतीति परोपकारी तस्य भावः ।",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "त्रितयम् । See com. and Pán. V. 2. 42. quoted therein.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r8",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 22. गजाङ्गनाया V. l.—गजस्य इव अञ्जनं गमनं यस्याः; with the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "gait of an elephant; hence a beautiful woman. If the reading",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
